<Group labelreference="L276" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">
<Font bold="true">generateHoloList</Font>
</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Code to generate a list of initial terms for a 'randomly' (Maple dependent) generated a series satisfying a holonomic ODE of order r and degree d 
Options for choosing dense or sparse ODEs, and defining the integer interval where initial conditions should be picked are also available.
An error may occur if Maple cannot compute the terms of the series solutions. 
When it takes too long to compute all the required series coefficients, it is preferable to stop the calculation and restart.
After the code zone below, we provide a code that can be ran several times until the number of required lists of coefficients is obtained.
</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field>
</Input>
</Group><CodeEditor-ExecGroup view="presentation" labelreference="L285" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" display="code"><EC-CodeEditor id="CodeEditRegion0" expanded="true" visible="true" pixel-width="500" pixel-height="200" code-language="text/maple" autofit="true" wrapping="true" show-border="true" code-line-numbers="true">generateHoloList := proc(r::posint,d::nonnegint,{denseORsparse::Or(identical(sparse),identical(dense)):=sparse,icsrange::[integer,integer]:=[0,100],displayHDE::truefalse:=false})
	local p,roll,Cy,HDE,ics,f_series,y::nothing,x::nothing,j;
	randomize();
	roll := rand(icsrange[1] .. icsrange[2]);
	p := randpoly([y], degree = r, denseORsparse, coeffs = (proc() randpoly(x, degree = d,denseORsparse); end proc));
	Order := (d + 1)*(r + 2) + r;
	Cy := PolynomialTools:-CoefficientList(p, y);
	HDE := add(Cy[j + 1]*diff(y(x), [x $ j]), j = 0 .. r) = 0;
	ics := {seq((D@@j)(y)(0) = roll(), j = 0 .. r - 1)};
	f_series := dsolve({HDE, op(ics)}, {y(x)}, series);
	f_series := eval(y(x), f_series);
	f_series := series(f_series, x, Order);
	if displayHDE then print(HDE) end if;
	return PolynomialTools:-CoefficientList(convert(f_series, polynom), x)
end proc:
